  "date": "2023-03",
  "title": "Morph Tales How Ai And Humans Interact",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "From the CAB to the ETH Main Building",
      "text": "Morph Tales combines an interactive augmented reality experience with a real campus experience at ETH Zurich. In a playful way, the game aims to give young people, families and adults an understanding of how artificial intelligence (AI) can support us in a wide range of activities, or how people and AI can work together to accomplish different tasks.\n\nThe game revolves around a likeable artificial intelligence named Morph, who is eager to learn and desperately needs the help of the players to realise its dream of becoming a reliable and trustworthy AI.\n\nMorph Tales is played with tablets at four gaming stations, where the players bring previously hidden worlds to life with augmented reality technology. After that, they help their Morph solve four tasks. The game lasts 20 to 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "heading": "From the CAB to the ETH Main Building",
      "text": "The full game will be available for play for the first time at the CAB building on 1 April 2023 as part of the Computer Science Days (find more information here ). After that, the game will remain in the CAB building until 14 April 2023 before being installed for the general public in the ETH Main Building on the Polyterrasse side. The game can be played at the CAB from 1 p.m. to 3 p.m. close to the food&lab restaurant, with no need to register.\n\nThis game was developed at ETH Zurich by the ETH Game Technology Center , the ETH AI Cente r and Corporate Communications on behalf of the ETH Executive Board. The four game challenges reflect four different AI research topics (smart farming, drug design, autonomous sailing, origin of life).\n\nThey are based on real ETH research projects from the Departments of Environmental Systems Science ( InnoFarm ), Chemistry and Applied Biosciences ( de novo drug design ), Information Technology and Electrical Engineering ( Autonomous Sailing ) and Earth Sciences ( Origins and Prevalence of Life , Geobiology ).\n\nThe game concept is also based on the approach of the ETH AI Center. The center focuses on collaborative, trustworthy, broadly accessible and inclusive AI systems that complement and do not replace humans in their tasks. Accordingly, the morphs in the game learn how to solve a task jointly with humans and reliably contribute their part."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Morph Tales in the CAB building at ETH",
      "text": "ETH Zurich Building CAB H 41 University Street 6 8092 Zurich"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Morph Tales at the Informatiktage 2023",
      "text": "Morph Tales will be presented at the Informatiktage 2023. The game can be found in the CAB building right next to the food&lab restaurant.\n\nAction day: Saturday, 1 April 2023, 09.30 - 17.00.\n\nIn the two weeks that follow the Computer Science Days, Morph Tales will remain in the CAB. Tablets will be handed out on site at the following times. Come by and train your Morph!"
    }
  ],
